module System/Memory

### Who a {Guarded[T, P]} lets in at the same time: its access policy. `ReadOnly` lets every reader in and has no
### writer, `Exclusive` one user at a time, `MultiRead` several readers or one writer.
###
### A policy holds the state of its access (who is in right now, which job holds it, how often and how long jobs
### waited), laid out as the runtime's AccessManager reads it. The `viewing` and `modifying` blocks take the access
### and give it up through the {GuardManager[T, P]}, which passes the policy's state to the AccessManager. The policy
### also decides at build time which blocks are legal: `ReadOnly` admits only `viewing`, `Exclusive` only
### `modifying`, `MultiRead` both.
###
### `P` is a type parameter of `Guarded`/`GuardManager`, so each policy is selected by monomorphization (no runtime
### dispatch): the manager's `access` member variable is laid out per `P` (`ReadOnly` is zero-sized).
### :see: {ReadOnly}, {Exclusive}, {MultiRead}, {Guarded}
protocol AccessPolicy
    ### Which access state the policy keeps, as the AccessManager knows it: 0 none (`ReadOnly`), 1 exclusive,
    ### 2 multi-read.
    @readonly
    routine Me.access_kind() -> U32
